text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'All creatures are black.', 'All creatures get -1/-1 until end of turn.', 'All lands are 2/2 creatures that are still lands.', 'As Engineered Plague enters the battlefield, choose a creature type.\\nAll creatures of the chosen type get -1/-1.', "As long as Static Orb is untapped, players can't untap more than two permanents during their untap steps.", "At the beginning of each player's draw step, if Howling Mine is untapped, that player draws an additional card.", "At the beginning of each player's draw step, that player puts the cards in their hand on the bottom of their library in any order, then draws that many cards.", "At the beginning of each player's end step, if that player didn't cast a spell this turn, Impatience deals 2 damage to that player.", 'At the beginning of your draw step, draw an additional card.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, discard your hand.', 'Attacking creatures you control get +1/+0.', "Beast of Burden's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creatures on the battlefield.", 'Black creatures get +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Blaze deals X damage to any target.', 'Cast this spell only during your end step.\\nAs an additional cost to cast this spell, pay X life.\\nDraw X cards.', 'Change the target of target spell with a single target.', 'Charcoal Diamond enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}.', 'Choose a color. Target player reveals their hand and discards all cards of that color.', 'Choose one —\\n• Target player gains 3 life.\\n• Prevent the next 3 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', 'Corrupt deals damage to any target equal to the number of Swamps you control. You gain life equal to the damage dealt this way.', 'Counter target creature spell.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.', 'Counter target spell.', "Counter target spell. If that spell is countered this way, put it on top of its owner's library instead of into that player's graveyard.", 'Creature spells cost {2} more to cast.', "Creatures can't block.", "Creatures with power 3 or greater don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", "Creatures with power greater than the number of cards in your hand can't attack.", 'Creatures you control get +0/+2 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'Creatures you control have first strike.', 'Creatures you control have flying.', 'Creatures you control have haste. (They can attack and {T} as soon as they come under your control.)', "Creatures you control have menace. (They can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nFirst strike", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nFlying", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nFlying\\nSunweb can't block creatures with power 2 or less.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{2}{U}{U}: Wall of Wonder gets +4/-4 until end of turn and can attack this turn as though it didn't have defender.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{B}: Regenerate Wall of Bone. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{R}: Wall of Fire gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", "Defender, flying (This creature can't attack, and it can block creatures with flying.)", 'Destroy X target nonblack creatures. Draw X cards.', 'Destroy all Islands.', 'Destroy all artifacts and enchantments.', "Destroy all creatures. They can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy all enchantments.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', "Destroy target artifact or land. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target artifact, enchantment, or land.', 'Destroy target artifact.', 'Destroy target creature with flying.', "Destroy target creature with power 4 or greater. It can't be regenerated.", "Destroy target land or nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target land.', "Destroy target nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target tapped creature.', 'Discard a land card: Seismic Assault deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Discard all the cards in your hand, then draw that many cards.', 'Disorder deals 2 damage to each white creature and each player who controls a white creature.', 'Draw four cards. You lose half your life, rounded up.', 'Each creature gets +1/+1 for each other creature on the battlefield that shares at least one creature type with it. (For example, if two Goblin Warriors and a Goblin Shaman are on the battlefield, each gets +2/+2.)', "Each creature you control can't be blocked by more than one creature.", "Each player can't cast more than one spell each turn.", 'Each player draws a card for each creature card in their graveyard.', "Each player may play an additional land during each of their turns.\\nWhenever a land is tapped for mana, return it to its owner's hand.", 'Each player sacrifices four lands. Wildfire deals 4 damage to each creature.', 'Earthquake deals X damage to each creature without flying and each player.', 'Enchant artifact\\nYou control enchanted artifact.', "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature has fear. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature has first strike. (It deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', 'Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals damage, you gain that much life.', "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\n{G}: Regenerate enchanted creature. (The next time that creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", 'Enchant creature\\nAll creatures able to block enchanted creature do so.', 'Enchant creature\\nAll damage that would be dealt to you is dealt to enchanted creature instead.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+0 for each Mountain you control.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 for each Forest you control.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+2.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+1.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has flying and vigilance.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has flying.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has swampwalk. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", 'Enchant land\\nWhenever enchanted land is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional {G}.', 'Enchant permanent\\nYou control enchanted permanent.', "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'Fire Diamond enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R}.', 'First strike', 'First strike; reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nFirst strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nNightmare's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Swamps you control.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever Thieving Magpie deals damage to an opponent, draw a card.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{1}{U}: Return Fleeting Image to its owner's hand.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{R}: Shivan Dragon gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", 'Flying, vigilance', "Flying\\nGoblin Glider can't block.", "Flying\\nRevenant's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creature cards in your graveyard.", 'Flying\\nSacrifice a creature: Fallen Angel gets +2/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhen Abyssal Horror enters the battlefield, target player discards two cards.', 'Flying\\nWhen Cloudchaser Eagle enters the battlefield, destroy target enchantment.', 'Flying\\nWhen Foul Imp enters the battlefield, you lose 2 life.', 'Flying\\nWhen Sage Owl enters the battlefield, look at the top four cards of your library, then put them back in any order.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Abyssal Specter deals damage to a player, that player discards a card.', "Flying\\nWhenever Bellowing Fiend deals damage to a creature, Bellowing Fiend deals 3 damage to that creature's controller and 3 damage to you.", 'Flying\\nWhenever Sustainer of the Realm blocks, it gets +0/+2 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{2}{U}: Untap Vigilant Drake.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Mawcor deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Target attacking or blocking creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Target attacking or blocking creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Target creature gains flying until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{X}, {T}: Crimson Hellkite deals X damage to target creature. Spend only red mana on X.', "Forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", "Goblin Raider can't block.", 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', 'Hurricane deals X damage to each creature with flying and each player.', 'If you control a creature, damage that would reduce your life total to less than 1 reduces it to 1 instead.', 'Inferno deals 6 damage to each creature and each player.', "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", 'Lava Axe deals 5 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'Lightning Blast deals 4 damage to any target.', "Look at target player's hand and choose two cards from it. Put them on top of that player's library in any order.", 'Look at the top seven cards of your library. Put two of them into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.', 'Look at the top two cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the other on the bottom of your library.', 'Marble Diamond enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}.', "Maro's power and toughness are each equal to the number of cards in your hand.", 'Moss Diamond enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}.', "Mountainwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", "Ogre Taskmaster can't block.", "Okk can't attack unless a creature with greater power also attacks.\\nOkk can't block unless a creature with greater power also blocks.", "Other Elf creatures get +1/+1 and have forestwalk. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Other Goblins get +1/+1 and have mountainwalk.', "Other Merfolk get +1/+1 and have islandwalk. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", "Phantom Warrior can't be blocked.", "Phyrexian Colossus doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nPay 8 life: Untap Phyrexian Colossus.\\nPhyrexian Colossus can't be blocked except by three or more creatures.", 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', 'Put target card from your graveyard on top of your library.', "Pygmy Pyrosaur can't block.\\n{R}: Pygmy Pyrosaur gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", 'Pyroclasm deals 2 damage to each creature.', 'Pyrotechnics deals 4 damage divided as you choose among any number of targets.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', "Return all creatures to their owners' hands.", "Return all green permanents to their owners' hands.", 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return target creature to its owner's hand.", "Return target permanent to its owner's hand.", 'Reveal the first card you draw each turn. Whenever you reveal a basic land card this way, draw a card.', 'Sacrifice Blood Pet: Add {B}.', 'Sacrifice any number of artifacts, creatures, and/or lands. Draw a card for each permanent sacrificed this way.', "Sea Monster can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Shock deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Sky Diamond enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U}.', "Spineless Thug can't block.", 'Spitting Earth deals damage to target creature equal to the number of Mountains you control.', 'Squall deals 2 damage to each creature with flying.', "Sudden Impact deals damage to target player equal to the number of cards in that player's hand.", "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", "Take an extra turn after this one. At the beginning of that turn's end step, you lose the game.", 'Tap all lands target player controls and that player loses all unspent mana.', 'Tap an untapped creature you control: Tap target artifact, creature, or land.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +7/+7 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +X/+0 until end of turn.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a creature card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a noncreature, nonland card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You draw a card for each Mountain and red card in it.', 'Target player discards three cards.', 'Target player discards two cards.', 'Target player draws four cards.', 'Target player draws two cards.', 'Target player gains X life.', 'Target player loses 4 life and you gain 4 life.', 'Target player untaps all basic lands they control.', 'The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage. You gain life equal to the damage prevented this way.', "Treefolk Seedlings's toughness is equal to the number of Forests you control.", 'Tremor deals 1 damage to each creature without flying.', "Uktabi Wildcats's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Forests you control.\\n{G}, Sacrifice a Forest: Regenerate Uktabi Wildcats.", 'Untap all creatures that attacked this turn. After this main phase, there is an additional combat phase followed by an additional main phase.', 'Untapped creatures you control get +0/+2.', 'Vigilance', 'Volcanic Hammer deals 3 damage to any target.', "Wall creatures can attack as though they didn't have defender.", 'When Dakmor Lancer enters the battlefield, destroy target nonblack creature.', 'When Delusions of Mediocrity enters the battlefield, you gain 10 life.\\nWhen Delusions of Mediocrity leaves the battlefield, you lose 10 life.', 'When Goblin Gardener dies, destroy target land.', 'When Goblin Matron enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a Goblin card, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Gravedigger enters the battlefield, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Serpent Warrior enters the battlefield, you lose 3 life.', 'When Staunch Defenders enters the battlefield, you gain 4 life.', "When Telepathic Spies enters the battlefield, look at target opponent's hand.", 'When Venerable Monk enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.', 'When Wood Elves enters the battlefield, search your library for a Forest card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Whenever City of Brass becomes tapped, it deals 1 damage to you.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Whenever Gang of Elk becomes blocked, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn for each creature blocking it.', 'Whenever Goblin Elite Infantry blocks or becomes blocked, it gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Hollow Dogs attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Seasoned Marshal attacks, you may tap target creature.', 'Whenever a Forest is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional {G}.', "Whenever a black card is put into an opponent's graveyard from anywhere, you may draw a card.", 'Whenever a creature attacks, Caltrops deals 1 damage to it.', 'Whenever a creature dies, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield, Aether Flash deals 2 damage to it.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield, its controller sacrifices a creature or land.', 'Whenever a green creature dies, its controller discards a card.', "Whenever a land is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, Dingus Egg deals 2 damage to that land's controller.", 'Whenever a player casts a black spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a blue spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a green spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a red spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a spell, that player discards a card.', "Whenever a player casts a spell, that player returns a land they control to its owner's hand.", 'Whenever a player casts a white spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a spell or ability an opponent controls causes a land to be put into your graveyard from the battlefield, return that card to the battlefield.', 'Whenever an Island an opponent controls becomes tapped, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a white spell, that player loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever an opponent discards a card, Megrim deals 2 damage to that player.', 'Whenever an opponent taps a Mountain for mana, you may gain 1 life.', "Whenever you cast a creature spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'Whenever you cast an enchantment spell, you may draw a card.', 'Yavimaya Enchantress gets +1/+1 for each enchantment on the battlefield.', "You and target opponent each flip a coin. Mana Clash deals 1 damage to each player whose coin comes up tails. Repeat this process until both players' coins come up heads on the same flip.", 'You gain 2 life for each card in your hand.', 'You gain 3 life for each black creature target opponent controls.', 'You gain 3 life for each creature attacking you.', 'You gain 4 life.', 'You have no maximum hand size.', "You may have Lone Wolf assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", "You may have Pride of Lions assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", "You may have Thorn Elemental assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", 'You may tap or untap target artifact, creature, or land.', 'Your opponents play with their hands revealed.', '{1}: The next time a black source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a blue source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a green source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a red source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a white source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}{G}: Regenerate Gorilla Chieftain.', '{1}{R}: Reckless Embermage deals 1 damage to any target and 1 damage to itself.', "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Pit Trap: Destroy target attacking creature without flying. It can't be regenerated.", '{2}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{2}, {T}: Target creature gains flying until end of turn.', '{2}, {T}: Target player mills two cards.', '{2}{U}{U}: Draw a card.', '{3}, {T}: Rod of Ruin deals 1 damage to any target.', '{3}, {T}: Target player discards a card. Activate only during your turn.', '{3}, {T}: Untap target creature.', '{3}: Patagia Golem gains flying until end of turn.', '{3}{G}, {T}: You may tap or untap target artifact, creature, or land.', '{4}, {T}: Draw a card.', "{8}, {T}: Aladdin's Ring deals 4 damage to any target.", '{B}, Pay 2 life: Draw a card.', '{B}: Looming Shade gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "{B}: Regenerate Drudge Skeletons. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", '{B}{B}, Pay 2 life, Sacrifice a Swamp: Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', '{B}{B}, {T}: Destroy target green creature.', '{B}{B}, {T}: Destroy target white creature.', '{B}{B}{B}, {T}: Target opponent reveals their hand and discards a creature card at random. Activate only during your turn.', '{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Elvish Lyrist: Destroy target enchantment.', '{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Scavenger Folk: Destroy target artifact.', '{G}, {T}: You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield.', "{G}: Regenerate Ancient Silverback. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", '{R}: Storm Shaman gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{T}, Sacrifice Daring Apprentice: Counter target spell.', '{T}, Sacrifice Ghitu Fire-Eater: It deals damage equal to its power to any target.', '{T}, Sacrifice Goblin Digging Team: Destroy target Wall.', "{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Bloodshot Cyclops deals damage equal to the sacrificed creature's power to any target.", '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Destroy target nonblack creature.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Sulfurous Springs deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}. Brushland deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}. Karplusan Forest deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Underground River deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}. Adarkar Wastes deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Add {G}{G}.', '{T}: All combat damage that would be dealt to you by unblocked creatures this turn is dealt to Kjeldoran Royal Guard instead.', '{T}: Crossbow Infantry deals 1 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', '{T}: Destroy target creature with power 4 or greater.', '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{T}: Draw a card.', '{T}: Elite Archers deals 3 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', '{T}: Femeref Archers deals 4 damage to target attacking creature with flying.', '{T}: Grapeshot Catapult deals 1 damage to target creature with flying.', '{T}: Heavy Ballista deals 2 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', '{T}: Orcish Artillery deals 2 damage to any target and 3 damage to you.', '{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{T}: Prevent the next 4 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{T}: Prodigal Sorcerer deals 1 damage to any target.', '{T}: Untap target creature.', "{U}{U}{U}, {T}: Return target permanent to its owner's hand.", '{W}: Honor Guard gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', '{W}{W}, {T}: Destroy target black permanent.', '{W}{W}, {T}: Destroy target red permanent.', '{X}: Crypt Rats deals X damage to each creature and each player. Spend only black mana on X.']
flavor: ['". . . Our castle\'s strength\\nWill laugh a siege to scorn."\\n—William Shakespeare,\\n*Macbeth*', '"A battle\'s outcome is never certain."\\n—The Southern Paladin', '"A flash of the lightning, a break of the wave,\\nHe passes from life to his rest in the grave."\\n—William Knox, "Mortality"', '"A stick is your friend. A pointed stick is your good friend. An army of pointed sticks is your best friend."\\n—Onean sergeant', '"Abandon ship!"', '"Be as fast as lightning, and you will be just as deadly."\\n—Combat trainer', '"Believe in the ideal, not the idol."\\n—Serra', '"Bet you can\'t put it through the eye."\\n"Left or right?"', '"Booga booga booga!"', '"Brackish water, dark and blind\\nHeed my will, to you I bind."\\n—Opening passage of Leshrac\'s Rite', '"Burn their homes. Salt their lands. Nothing survives."\\n—The Western Paladin', '"But high she shoots through air and light,\\nAbove all low delay,\\nWhere nothing earthly bounds her flight,\\nNor shadow dims her way."\\n—Thomas Moore,\\n"Oh that I had Wings"', '"Catch!"', '"Change your mind, or I\'ll change it for you."', '"Defeating an enemy is not nearly as satisfying as watching one suffer."\\n—The Western Paladin', '"Dig. Dig. Dig. Dig. Dig. Dig. Die!"\\n—Goblin chant', '"East and West meet and angels cry.\\nUnholy power darkens the sky."\\n—"The Ballad of the Paladins"', '"Eri phar phesta . . . um, phistor . . . er, phistara . . ."', '"Even in the darkest night\\nStars and angels still shine bright."\\n—Onean children\'s rhyme', '"Every day, I fight for my life and win. Every night, I fight to remember my name and lose."', '"Expect nothing but scorn, flattery, and lies. And never turn your back on him."\\n—The Northern Paladin', '"Fear this no more!"', '"Fire hurts them almost as much as the chaos that follows. Almost."\\n—The Western Paladin', '"For he on honey-dew hath fed,\\nAnd drunk the milk of Paradise."\\n—Samuel Taylor Coleridge,\\n"Kubla Khan"', '"For what are leaves but countless blades\\nTo fight a countless foe on high."\\n—Elvish hymn', '"From the snowy slopes of Kaelor,\\nTo the canyons of Bandu,\\nWe drink and fight and feast and die\\nAs we were born to do."\\n—Balduvian tavern song', '"Give it a week and it will feed an army."', '"Guess where I\'m gonna plant this!"', '"Hence \'banishèd\' is banished from the world, / And the world\'s exile is death."\\n—William Shakespeare,\\n*Romeo and Juliet*', '"Here, kitty kitty. Here, kitty kitty. Aaaaugh!"', '"How can anyone fight so much yet enjoy it so little?"\\n—The Western Paladin', '"How many people can you save in that thing?"\\n"All of them," replied the mage with a smile.', '"How smooth his face, how sure his thoughts. I look forward to breaking his mighty will."\\n—The Eastern Paladin', '"I don\'t *feel* any different."', '"I don\'t *think* so."', '"I dreamt of it once. Now I fear it dreams of me."\\n—Tolarian scholar', '"I felt the ground shake, so I hid in my tent until the earthquake passed. It passed all right, and it left hoofprints."\\n—Femeref explorer', '"I may seem wise to you, but I\'m merely a sapling among mighty oaks."', '"I rely not so much on the wisdom of age as on the overconfidence of youth."', '"I think little of the foes I\'ve slain. But I\'m haunted by the friends I\'ve sent to die."\\n—The Southern Paladin', '"I want every last one of these tree-hugging, earth-loving, pointy-eared weaklings out of here. Now!"', '"I wouldn\'t stand in front of that wurm, son. \'Course, I wouldn\'t stand behind it neither. In fact, standing anywhere near that wurm\'s not much of a plan. Running, now *that\'s* a plan!"\\n—Wandering mage', '"I\'ll climb down soon. Don\'t worry, it\'s just a thundersto—"\\n—Former elvish scout', '"I\'m going to count to three. Three."', '"I\'m not one for pretty things," said Sisay. "Unless they\'re pretty useful as well."', '"I\'ve seen my master do this a hundred times. How hard can it be?"', '"If not for the wizard, we\'d all be dead now. \'Course, it was him that started all this in the first place."\\n—Onean veteran', '"It is a slaughter, the death of a sea. Never speak of it again."\\n—The Lord of Atlantis', '"It is the duty of the strong to oppose any who threaten the weak."\\n—The Southern Paladin', '"It is useful to be able to speak to the trees. But it is truly wondrous to be able to listen to them."', '"It was as if we fought a shadow."\\n—Onean soldier', '"It\'s a poor sort of memory that only works backwards."\\n—Lewis Carroll,\\n*Through the Looking Glass*', '"It\'s hard to keep our own troops from fleeing when he\'s like this. How can our foes possibly stand against him?"\\n—Field marshal for the Eastern Paladin', '"Knowledge is a feast for the mind. Savor every swallow."', '"Knowledge is power."\\n—Sir Francis Bacon,\\n*Meditationes Sacrae*', '"Let me introduce you to Rocky."', '"Let the air itself protect you, for it is everywhere."\\n—Master wizard', '"May the winds blow till they have wakened death. . . ."\\n—William Shakespeare,\\n*Othello*', '"Mercy? Mercy is for the playground, not the battleground."', '"Most people believe magic is only a trick. Why change their minds?"', '"Nope, there\'s nothing here either. You guys go on ahead, I\'ll catch up in a minute. . . . Whoo hoo!"', '"North and South meet and angels sing.\\nVoices resound with a righteous ring."\\n—"The Ballad of the Paladins"', '"Nothing can stop the power of life—not even death."\\n—Onean cleric', '"Of course she\'s at the head of her class. All of her classmates have disappeared."\\n—Tolarian renegade', '"One piece? Now there\'s a hundred!"', '"Ready . . . aim . . . fire!"\\n"Ow!"', '"Remove their power, and their will to fight will follow."\\n—Tolarian wizard', '"Returne from whence ye came. . . ."\\n—Edmund Spenser,\\n*The Faerie Queene*', '"Secrets? What secrets?"', '"Soldiers wear down and enemies collapse—but the ballista never tires."\\n—Ballista captain', '"Some have said there is no subtlety to destruction. You know what? They\'re dead."\\n—Wandering mage', '"That arm\'s for bashin\'. That one\'s for smashin\'. That one\'s for scratchin\'. And that one . . . I don\'t know what that one\'s for."\\n—Orgg trainer', '"The dead make good soldiers. They can\'t disobey orders, they never surrender, and they don\'t stop fighting when a random body part falls off."\\n—Nevinyrral,\\n*Necromancer\'s Handbook*', '"The dead whisper to the living. If you listen, you will learn."\\n—Maro', '"The key to winning any fight is simply staying alive."\\n—The Southern Paladin', '"The paladins would be wise not to forget about the Pearl Trident. The merfolk warriors have turned the tide of more than one human war . . . and I have no doubt they shall do so again."\\n—Onean scholar', '"The peasants labor for my profit. I approve."', '"The surface world contains nothing I cannot take."\\n—The Lord of Atlantis', '"Their thoughts flow through my mind, and I am healed."\\n—Fyndhorn elder', '"There is no worse enemy. His passion for death doesn\'t just border on insanity, it wallows in it."\\n—The Southern Paladin', '"There\'s never been a dwarven smith who could match the marvels that Gaea herself forges."\\n—The Elvish Champion', '"They groaned, they stirred, they all uprose,\\nNor spake, nor moved their eyes;\\nIt had been strange, even in a dream,\\nTo have seen those dead men rise."\\n—Samuel Taylor Coleridge,\\n"The Rime of the Ancient Mariner"', '"Training? Seeing my crops burnt to cinders was all the \'training\' I needed."', '"We have no need for these trinkets. We need only the strength of our swords and the virtue of our hearts."\\n—The Northern Paladin', '"We live for a thousand years. The death of even one brings untold sorrow."\\n—Elvish elder', '"We spent three weeks trying to knock that wall down. Now it\'s knocking us down."\\n—Onean sergeant', '"We were ready for an attack from the front, sides, or back—but the mage hit us from below."\\n—Veteran soldier', '"We\'ll be easy targets if we remain on the ground. Let\'s take the fight to them."', '"Weapons usually bring death. Today, mine will bring life."', '"What\'s got two arms, one wing, and no brains?"\\n—Ghitu riddle', '"Wheeeeeeeeeeeeeee!"', '"When the air burns, only death breathes deep."\\n—Bogardan mage', '"When the forest wants something, no mortal mind can resist her."\\n—Maro', '"Who says lightning never strikes twice?"\\n—Storm shaman', '"Why do you weep for the dead? I rejoice, for they have died for me."\\n—Fallen angel, to Serra', '"Why should death always have the last word?"\\n—Llanowar druid', '"With one breath, the newborn angel took to the air . . . and the world sighed."\\n—*The Book of Serra*', '"You won\'t be needing this."', '"You\'ve thrown your net at the wrong fish."\\n—The Lord of Atlantis', 'A bored wizard once created a vizzerdrix out of a bunny and a piranha. He never made *that* mistake again.', 'A fool knows no fear. A hero shows no fear.', 'A fruit must rot before its seed can sprout.\\n—Yavimaya saying', 'A full coffin is like a full coffer—both are attractive to thieves.', 'A gorilla chief must always be prepared to defend his crown. This leads to some pretty tough apes.', 'A hollow dog is never empty. It is filled with thirst for the hunt.', 'A master of tactics, the Lord of Atlantis makes his people bold in battle merely by arriving to lead them.', 'A picture is worth a thousand swords.', "A reward is worthless if you aren't around to enjoy it.", 'A single germ can kill more soldiers than ten thousand blades.', 'A skeletal wall, strengthened by the souls of traitors, rings the city of the Eastern Paladin.', "A valiant knight's life has no meaning without honor.", 'A wolf without a pack is either a survivor or a brute.', 'After their first encounter, the goblins named him Chuck.', 'An advisor once asked the Western Paladin how much gold would be enough. "I have no need of fools who can imagine \'enough,\'" he told the advisor\'s corpse.', "An angel's blessing prepares a soldier for war better than a thousand military drills.", 'And would you strip the bark from a treefolk?\\n—Elvish expression meaning "Are you crazy?"', 'Armodons are trained to step on things. Enemy things.', 'As the foul beast appeared, arcane lightning crackled around it.', 'Beware anything born among the dead.\\n—Tolarian saying', 'Blessed by a thousand prayers.', 'Bridges usually get you from one place to another. This one just gets you.', 'Caught red-handed.', 'Do not judge a lizard by its size.\\n—Ghitu proverb', 'Each spell has its own song, and the enchantress knows the dance for each.', 'Earth arms itself with fire.', 'Even the grandest forest begins with a single seedling.\\n—Llanowar saying', 'Every branch a crossroads, every vine a swift steed.', 'Exhausting a wizard can be exhausting work.', 'Feroz is gone, but what remains is his final gift to his people: the right to be left alone.', 'Fire finds its form in the heat of the forge.', 'Fire is always at the top of the food chain, and it has a *big* appetite.', 'Fire never dies alone.', 'Forged by a thousand flames.', "From Gaea grew the world, and the world was silent. From Gaea grew the world's elves, and the world was silent no more.\\n—Elvish teaching", 'Get in touch with your inner monster.', 'Goblins prefer caves to just about anything else. Caves prefer just about anything else to goblins.', 'Grief is a razor that slices the soul.', 'He can drown you in his eyes.', 'He hunts what might have been.', 'He raged at the world, at his family, at his life. But mostly he just raged.', 'He reads the battlefield like a map, always seeking the shortest route to victory.', 'He wastes his amazing talents on proving how amazing he really is.', "He's smart for a goblin. He can do *two* things: hit *and* run.", "Her heart holds the pain of every soldier she's ever healed.", "Her roots connect her to the forest's wishes.", 'Her sword sings more beautifully than any choir.', 'Hill giants are mostly just big. Of course, that does count for a lot.', 'Honorable in battle, generous in death.\\n—Motto of the Kjeldoran Royal Guard', 'If only every message were as perfect as its messenger.', 'If you stop to listen, you can hear it grow.', "It can pass through solid matter—but that doesn't mean it's harmless.", 'It can stay aloft for weeks with little or no sleep.', "It doesn't like having visitors . . . unless it's having them for lunch.", "It doesn't think. It doesn't feel.\\nIt doesn't laugh or cry.\\nAll it does from dusk till dawn\\nIs make the soldiers die.\\n—Onean children's rhyme", 'It eats death and drinks pain.', 'It keeps the upper reaches of the forest free of every menace . . . except for the spider itself.', 'It treads on feet of coals and strikes with the force of a volcano.', 'Its wings were only designed to be ornamental, but it learned to use them on its own.', "Kings don't make knights. Actions do.", 'Knights are quick to pledge their loyalty and even quicker to charge into battle.', 'Knights fight for honor and mercenaries fight for gold. The militia fights for hearth and home.', 'Knowledge knows no bounds.', 'Legend has it that the mine howls out the last words of those who died inside.', 'Legend has it that the world was hatched from a dingus egg.', 'Like a meteor, it strikes from above without warning. Unlike a meteor, it then carries you off and eats you.', 'Like arguing with ice\\n—Vodalian expression meaning "wasting your time"', "Little things like morals shouldn't hinder one's ambition.\\n—Pirate creed", 'Llanowar covers a million square miles, yet nobody enters the forest without the elves knowing it.', 'Memories cut from the mind can cut right back.', 'Mold crept over the walls and into every crevice until the gleaming white stone strained and burst.', 'More than any other battlefield, the forest gives the advantage to those who know it best.', 'More than one mage has been driven insane by the sound of the millstone relentlessly grinding away.', 'Most books simply deliver knowledge. This one expects some in return.', 'Most eagles hunt small animals. The cloudchasers hunt magic.', 'Most spies sneak into enemy camps. These spies sneak into enemy minds.', 'Nature grows solutions to her problems.', "Neither head holds a brain—that's located somewhere in the chest—but four eyes aim much better than two.", 'Never forget your feet\\n—Elvish expression meaning "watch your step"', 'No fear. No sense. And soon, no lunch.', "No forest is so remote that the elves don't know its secrets.", 'No one knows whether they were named for the diseases they carry or for the speed at which they multiply.', 'No thrull has ever been burdened with a long life.', 'No two see the same Maro.', 'Of royal blood among the spirits of the air, the Mahamoti djinn rides on the wings of the winds. As dangerous in the gambling hall as he is in battle, he is a master of trickery and misdirection.', 'Ogres learn how to smash stuff even before they learn how to walk.', 'On darkness feeding, in nightmares breeding.', 'Other birds collect twigs for their nests. Magpies steal jewels for theirs.', 'Pockets of Æther can be so foul they melt flesh from bone.', 'Polished by a thousand waves.', 'Rain from this storm leaves you pinned to the ground like an insect.', 'Scholars in their ivory towers call them "sharks of the sky." Scholars on the road don\'t call them at all.', 'Seek balance in all things—as long as the scales are weighted in your favor.\\n—Vodalian saying', 'Seekers spend their lives protecting a home they rarely visit.', 'Sharper than wind, lighter than air.', 'She speaks with the voice of the winds, and the earth trembles.', "Some say Aladdin's third wish was for this ring.", 'Some say they have the blood of hawks running through their veins.', 'Sometimes the wings of fallen dragons refuse to give up the sky.', 'Spring breathes the magic of new life.', 'Storm crow descending, winter unending. Storm crow departing, summer is starting.', 'Strengthened by a thousand limbs.', 'Tainted by a thousand fears.', "The Eastern Paladin doesn't attack at night for the tactical advantage. He does it for the sheer joy of fighting beneath the moon.", 'The Eastern Paladin knew how highly his southern rival valued horses, so he gleefully prepared a suitable welcome.', "The Ghitu believe their race was born of fire, and it's an honor to return to it.", "The Phyrexian killing machines couldn't have known the seriousness of their mistake in wounding the ape—they'd never seen it angry.", 'The Southern Paladin taught the airborne vermin to fear the storm that rains upward.', 'The archers have a reputation for attacking without warning. They claim that the first arrow *is* the warning.', 'The assassin sees only throats and hears only heartbeats.', "The battle's end is the meal's beginning.", 'The bigger they are, the stronger its pull.', 'The bodies of its victims are the only tracks it leaves.', "The bog's touch means death to all but the darkest of hearts.", 'The coral merfolk delight in wrestling with their foes, skinning them alive on the razor-sharp edges of their reef.', 'The darkness of his shield reflects the inky blackness of his soul.', 'The deep sleep of winter is not always restful.', 'The earliest mystics believed that the falcon slit the sky to let the light break through.', 'The earth cannot hold that which magic commands.', 'The eclipse made it clear whose side the sky was on.', 'The elves long ago mastered the art of hunting with nets. They call it "fishing the sky."', 'The erupting flames work as both barrier and weapon.', 'The generals were dead. The battle plans were forgotten. It was everyone for themselves.', 'The goblin idea of music is to hit something with a stick.', 'The hardest part of his training is learning not to eat the boar.', 'The heavier the load, the harder it works.', 'The hellkites are artists with flames, painting the world with fire.', 'The intensity of their glare was soon surpassed by the intensity of their attack.', 'The land rises up to defend against those who would spoil its beauty.', 'The land will never betray those who gave their lives for it.', 'The mana that binds the world together can also tear it apart.', 'The merfolk may rule the waters, but hippos have never had much respect for authority.', 'The noble paladins draw strength from the courage of others.', 'The only thing that flows faster than water is fear.', 'The rod is a relic from ancient times . . . cruel, vicious, mean-spirited times.', 'The sea has many secrets, but some are too big to be kept.', 'The sky is her stage.', 'The strength of one. The courage of ten.', 'The thunder of its hooves beats dreams into despair.', 'The undisputed master of the mountains of Shiv.', 'The villagers call it "winged stench."', "The warping of bodies and souls has become the heart of Yawgmoth's existence.", 'The warriors fought against the paralyzing waves until even their thoughts froze in place.', 'The wise pay as much attention to what they throw away as to what they keep.', "There's only one thing worse than a hungry lion—many hungry lions.", "They fight so closely together a mouse couldn't slip past their guard.", 'They fletch their arrows with the feathers of angels.', 'They wondered at the size of it. It wondered which to eat first.', "They'll chew through armor, flesh, and bone. They'll even chew through each other if they're hungry enough.", "They're the fiercest of all the Western Paladin's soldiers. They're also the most fiercely loyal—but that loyalty comes at a price.", "They've got claws as long as your arm. And they're grouchy. Really, really grouchy.", 'Think of it as a butcher knife with wings.', 'Those who play with fire are bound to get burned.', 'Those who understand the forest are free to harvest its bounty.', 'To an elf, magic and music are the same.', 'To be king, Numsgil did in Blog, who did in Unkful, who did in Viddle, who did in Loll, who did in Alrok. . . .', 'To gaze under its hood is to invite death.', 'Too many wizards spoil the spell, but too many spells spoil the wizard.\\n—Sign on entry to arcane lab', "Toren had stepped on a lot of bugs during his life, so he couldn't help feeling embarrassed when a bug stepped on him.", "Twang. You're dead.", 'Watching the spider\'s web\\n—Llanowar expression meaning "focusing on the wrong thing"', "We're *elite*. You're not.\\n—Infantry motto", 'What it lacks in backbone, it makes up for in cruelty.', 'What wizards fear most is losing their minds.', 'When nothing but second best will do.', 'When the strands call, only the dead answer.', "When you sink a lot of ships, it's easy to find sunken treasure.", 'Where do you run when the earth becomes your enemy?', 'Where dryads dance, seeds sprout and flowers bloom.', 'Where psycho meets cyclone.', "Whether it howls for hunger or for joy, you're in trouble just the same.", 'Why does a Samite heal? You might as well ask why a bird flies.', 'Why not ask the winds?\\n—Tolarian expression meaning "Who knows?"', 'Without warriors there can be no war.', 'Years of attempts have brought the goblins no closer to growing a sausage tree.', 'You are who you eat.', "You may break her shield, but you'll never break her spirit.", "You'll never find an anaconda in a swamp. It will always find you first.", "Your heart's desire is found within.\\n—Saddlebag inscription"]
